{"duration_api_ms":21582,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"37706a37-72e4-4811-99cb-007595d14758","total_cost_usd":0.050696599999999994,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1615,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1870,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":373},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1615,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1870,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1615,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1615},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":2181,"outputTokens":301,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.00036860000000000007,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":274,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":1870,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":1615,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.050328,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":373,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":1615,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"```json\n{\"id\":\"QL-34\",\"points\":[{\"point\":1,\"mark\":\"required\",\"minimum\":\"States that an Irish UCITS ETF must disclose its portfolio transparency policy and where portfolio and/or iNAV information can be found, and ties this disclosure obligation to the 2026 regulations (Reg. 88(3)-(4)). Listing the specific documents is optional: the prospectus is the minimum, and the KID/KIID and marketing materials are nice-to-have. Exact regulation paragraph numbers are optional if the source is identified as the 2026 regulations.\"},{\"point\":2,\"mark\":\"required\",\"minimum\":\"Distinguishes two permitted routes under CBI Q&A 1012 (April 2025). (a) Daily portfolio holdings disclosed publicly on a non-discriminatory basis. (b) Periodic holdings disclosure, permitted only if daily arbitrage-relevant information is made available on a non-discriminatory basis to APs/market makers. Minimum conditions for route (b): the daily arbitrage information is available to all APs/market makers, not selectively; and public quarter-end holdings are published, with the 30-business-day deadline stated or substantially stated. Full credit also needs at least one further safeguard from: prospectus disclosure of the arbitrage information supplied; procedures for when arbitrage is impaired; procedures for handling investor information requests. Listing all three safeguards is optional but expected for an exemplary answer. Page cites are optional. Half-credit (partial) if both routes are distinguished but most conditions of the periodic route are missing, e.g. only the non-discriminatory AP information is mentioned.\"},{\"point\":3,\"mark\":\"required\",\"minimum\":\"Makes clear that the transparency-policy disclosure obligations in point 1 apply under both routes. Also makes clear that the periodic route is conditional, depending on the daily AP/market-maker arbitrage information and documented procedures, and is not an unconditional alternative. Optional subdetails: holdings disclosure identifies securities/positions and quantities; the prospectus states what information is supplied under the chosen route; if an iNAV is calculated, the prospectus explains its methodology and calculation frequency; the contrast with US Rule 6c-11 (daily public full holdings not mandatory in Ireland). Omitting the optional subdetails is not penalised. If only one of the two minimum elements is present, the point earns half-credit.\"}],\"central_errors\":[\"Stating that Irish UCITS ETFs must publish full portfolio holdings publicly every day, with no periodic alternative, i.e. importing the US Rule 6c-11 requirement as mandatory.\",\"Stating that the periodic-holdings route lets the ETF withhold all daily portfolio/arbitrage information, or treating periodic disclosure as unconditional.\",\"Stating that daily arbitrage information may be given selectively or preferentially to chosen APs/market makers, rather than on a non-discriminatory basis.\",\"Stating that the transparency-policy/prospectus disclosure obligations fall away or do not apply under the periodic route.\",\"Stating that no public periodic holdings disclosure is required under the periodic route. Also wrong: giving a materially different frequency or deadline (e.g. annual only, or no deadline) instead of quarter-end within 30 business days.\",\"Presenting the daily and periodic routes as the same requirement, or failing to distinguish them, while asserting a single regime that contradicts the supplied sources.\"],\"scoring_rule\":{\"correct\":\"All three points meet their stated minimums, and no central error is present. Optional subdetails such as the KID/marketing listing, the iNAV methodology, the full safeguard list, citations and the US comparison are not required for full credit.\",\"partial\":\"No central error is present, but at least one required point falls short of its minimum. Examples: a point earns only half-credit as defined in its minimum, or point 3's conditionality/both-routes element is missing. If at least one required point is fully met and the rest are half-met or missing, score partial. Omissions alone never make an answer wrong. Imprecise but non-contradictory detail (e.g. 'about a month' instead of '30 business days') counts as partial for that element.\",\"wrong\":\"The answer asserts any central error as part of its substantive answer, even if other points are covered. It is also wrong if it fails to meet the minimum of both point 1 and point 2, i.e. it neither identifies the transparency-policy disclosure obligation nor distinguishes the daily and conditional periodic routes.\"}}\n```","ttft_ms":4800,"type":"result","duration_ms":19949,"uuid":"9008201c-540d-4992-adab-9b179144ca21","ttft_stream_ms":1082,"time_to_request_ms":60,"first_content_frame_ms":1083,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
